  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Monday)\nIssued at 1234 PM MDT Tue Sep 15 2026\n\nThe upper low will move toward the tri-state area of CA/OR/NV on\nThursday, causing the monsoon moisture plume to tilt a bit more \nsouthwest to northeast, but high PWATs (1.0 to 1.2 inch) will \nremain over most of NM. This will steer the best focus for storms \ndivergently from the Gila into all of northern NM with a secondary\nfocus over the south central to central mountains/highlands. \nStorm motions would not alter much, and antecedent conditions \nwill likely dictate where any Flood Watches get issued, but at \nthis point there seems to be a moderate to high likelihood (50-70%\nchance) of one being issued for western NM zones on Thursday. \n\nWith the low moving a bit farther inland over northwestern states\non Friday, the flow will gain a very slight westerly component in\nNM, potentially leading to some drier air in northwestern zones.\nBlended ensemble means support some drying in northwestern zones,\nbut the ECMWF family seems more reluctant to dry things out. This\nmoisture gradient could enhance development, but nailing down the\nexact placement is tricky at this point. Scattered to numerous \nshowers and storms have been left in the forecast for most western\nand central zones, but western areas may be due for significant \ntrimming on subsequent shifts if current trends hold. \n\nThe westerlies still look to overtake more of the forecast area \ninto Saturday, inhibiting the rainfall efficiency and reducing the\nnumber of storms, particularly in western zones. The \naforementioned low would be moving into the northern Rockies, \nperhaps providing faint forcing and lift for anything in central\nto eastern NM.\n\nBy Sunday, there is increasing consensus that lighter and drier\nnorthwest flow aloft will build into NM with an overall continued\ndecrease in storm coverage for most zones. Northeastern NM would \nbe an exception, as another weak, but moist backdoor front is \nslated to invade. \n\nA weak upper trough is modeled with poor agreement on placement \nby Monday. Storms would likely favor eastern NM based on Sunday's \nbackdoor front, and confidence is low that there will be \nsufficient moisture elsewhere.",
